# Storage

The server keeps artifacts (uploaded model files, datasets, and other card payloads) in an object store, separate from Postgres. Pick one backend with `WYRD_STORAGE_BACKEND` and set that backend's variables. Four backends are supported: `local`, `s3`, `gcs`, and `azure`.

Credentials for the cloud backends come from each provider's standard SDK credential chain, not from Wyrd-specific secrets. You configure the bucket and region through Wyrd, and let the cloud SDK resolve the identity the way it does everywhere else (environment, instance role, workload identity).

## Shared settings

These apply to every backend.

| Variable | Default | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `WYRD_STORAGE_BACKEND` | none (required) | `local`, `s3`, `gcs`, or `azure`. |
| `WYRD_STORAGE_REQUIRE_ENCRYPTION` | `false` | Require an encryption marker when an upload completes. |
| `WYRD_STORAGE_PRESIGN_TTL_SECS` | `600` | Presigned URL lifetime. Clamped to `60`–`3600`. |
| `WYRD_STORAGE_PART_SIZE_BYTES` | `16777216` (16 MiB) | Multipart part size. Must be MiB-aligned. Clamped to 5 MiB–5 GiB. |
| `WYRD_STORAGE_MULTIPART_THRESHOLD_BYTES` | `104857600` (100 MiB) | Object size at or above which cloud backends switch to multipart upload. |

## Local

Files on the server's own disk. Fine for development and single-node setups, not for a horizontally scaled deployment where replicas do not share a filesystem.

| Variable | Required | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `WYRD_STORAGE_LOCAL_ROOT` | yes | Absolute path to the storage root. Must exist. |
| `WYRD_PUBLIC_BASE_URL` | yes | Public base URL of the server, used to build artifact links. |

```bash
export WYRD_STORAGE_BACKEND=local
export WYRD_STORAGE_LOCAL_ROOT=/var/lib/wyrd/artifacts
export WYRD_PUBLIC_BASE_URL=https://wyrd.internal
```

## S3

Amazon S3 or any S3-compatible store (MinIO, Ceph, R2). Credentials resolve through the AWS default credential chain: environment variables, IAM role, instance metadata, and so on. Wyrd does not take an access key directly.

| Variable | Required | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `WYRD_STORAGE_S3_BUCKET` | yes | Bucket name, no `s3://` prefix. |
| `WYRD_STORAGE_S3_REGION` | no | AWS region. Falls back to the SDK default chain if unset. |
| `WYRD_STORAGE_S3_ENDPOINT_URL` | no | Custom endpoint for an S3-compatible store. Forces path-style addressing. |
| `WYRD_STORAGE_S3_FORCE_PATH_STYLE` | no | Force path-style addressing without setting a custom endpoint. |

```bash
export WYRD_STORAGE_BACKEND=s3
export WYRD_STORAGE_S3_BUCKET=wyrd-artifacts
export WYRD_STORAGE_S3_REGION=us-east-1
# Credentials via the AWS default chain (env, IAM role, instance metadata).
```

## GCS

Google Cloud Storage. Credentials resolve in order: inline service account JSON, a service account key file, then Application Default Credentials (gcloud config, Workload Identity).

| Variable | Required | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `WYRD_STORAGE_GCS_BUCKET` | yes | Bucket name, no `gs://` prefix. |
| `WYRD_STORAGE_GCS_ENDPOINT_URL` | no | Custom endpoint or emulator. |

Credential variables (first match wins):

| Variable | Notes |
| --- | --- |
| `GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS_JSON` | Inline service account JSON. |
| `GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS` | Path to a service account key file. |
| (Application Default Credentials) | gcloud config or Workload Identity, used if neither of the above is set. |

```bash
export WYRD_STORAGE_BACKEND=gcs
export WYRD_STORAGE_GCS_BUCKET=wyrd-artifacts
export GOOGLE_APPLICATION_CREDENTIALS=/run/secrets/gcs-sa.json
```

## Azure

Azure Blob Storage. Credentials resolve through the Azure default credential chain (`AZURE_CLIENT_ID`, `AZURE_CLIENT_SECRET`, `AZURE_TENANT_ID`, managed identity). For an emulator like Azurite, set the account key directly with `AZURE_STORAGE_ACCOUNT_KEY`.

| Variable | Required | Notes |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `WYRD_STORAGE_AZURE_ACCOUNT` | yes | Storage account name. |
| `WYRD_STORAGE_AZURE_CONTAINER` | yes | Blob container name. |
| `WYRD_STORAGE_AZURE_ENDPOINT_URL` | no | Custom endpoint. Defaults to `https://{account}.blob.core.windows.net`. |

```bash
export WYRD_STORAGE_BACKEND=azure
export WYRD_STORAGE_AZURE_ACCOUNT=wyrdstorage
export WYRD_STORAGE_AZURE_CONTAINER=artifacts
# Credentials via the Azure default chain, or AZURE_STORAGE_ACCOUNT_KEY for an emulator.
```

